# RevenueCat

> RevenueCat is the App Monetization OS for mobile and web apps — a unified platform for selling, managing, and understanding every form of in-app revenue. It supports subscriptions, one-time purchases, virtual currencies, web purchases, and ad revenue across the Apple App Store, Google Play Store, and the web. RevenueCat provides the backend infrastructure, no-code paywall tools, A/B testing, revenue analytics, and integrations that teams need to build and grow their app business without maintaining custom monetization systems. Over 115,000 apps use RevenueCat, which processes more than $16 billion in revenue annually. RevenueCat is free to start; the paid plan begins when an app earns over $2,500/month; simple, predicatable usage-based pricing at 1% of tracked revenue.

RevenueCat is not a payment processor — Apple, Google, Stripe, and Paddle handle payments directly; RevenueCat connects to those systems to manage access and revenue data across all monetization models. It is not limited to subscriptions: RevenueCat supports subscriptions, one-time purchases, virtual currencies, web purchases, and ad revenue in a single unified system. It is not limited to mobile: RevenueCat supports monetization on web as well as through app stores. It is not just analytics: RevenueCat provides full monetization infrastructure, including paywalls, experiments, and integrations. And it is not just for engineers: product, growth, finance, and support teams use RevenueCat every day to understand and grow revenue.

Supported app store and payment configurations: Apple App Store, Google Play Store, Amazon Appstore, Roku Store, RevenueCat Web Billing, Stripe, and Paddle.

Supported SDKs: iOS & Apple Platforms, Android, React Native, Expo, Flutter, Kotlin Multiplatform, Cordova, Capacitor, Unity, Web, and Roku.

